From 928a9f3b7043c3d315f9509c0884e9609c4d1d27 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Tianyu9748 <54686548+Tianyu9748@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 17:18:06 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 09/26] [Diffusion] Causal KV seam: resident session KV across
 requests

Archival runs behind generation, so a backend can keep a session's native
KV resident between requests instead of restoring it from the archive.
The stages already keep their caches across requests and only reset the
cursors; what was missing is a way to tell that nothing wrote the K/V
since (inference tensors have no version counter).

* CausalSelfAttentionKVCache.mutation_generation: a process-unique tag
  renewed by every method that writes k/v (update, growth, restore
  install), never by cursor/pin changes.
* index_state() / holds_index_state() / restore_index_state(): record the
  cursors, pinned shot sink and geometry at the end of a request and
  reinstate them over unchanged K/V (ValueError otherwise).
* causal_kv_session gains an optional bool "durable": whether the request
  returns only once its chunks are archived (backend default otherwise).

Co-authored-by: Copilot <223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>
